%% Agent harness architecture. This is the source of truth; architecture.png
%% is rendered from it:
%%   npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i docs/architecture.mmd \
%%     -o docs/architecture.png -w 2400 -s 2
%% ---
%% What attaches around the loop, and where:
%% ---
%%   * Observability. Every metric section 8.4 asks for is derived from
%%     lifecycle callbacks the loop already fired, so telemetry is a Hook
%%     like any other and the fourteen original metric names are frozen
%%     against the Grafana dashboard (ADR-081).
%% ---
%%     The layer was rebuilt around a SPAN MODEL (ADR-093). There were two
%%     observers — one for metrics, one for the trace file — each with its
%%     own stopwatches and each needing an edit to record a new field. Now
%%     ONE hook opens spans and the Tracer fans finished spans out to three
%%     exporters. A new telemetry field is one attribute in one place, and
%%     a dashboard and a trace file cannot disagree about a run because
%%     they read the same object.
%% ---
%%     Spans NEST, which the flat event log could not express: a permission
%%     decision is a child of the tool call it governed rather than the
%%     line printed next to it, and a delegated child run is a subtree of
%%     the parent's delegate call. Every failure carries an error.type and
%%     the layer responsible for it (ADR-094).
%%   * A skill-scoped permission wrapper. There is still exactly one gate,
%%     consulted before every tool call (ADR-057). A loaded skill's
%%     allowed-tools narrows it and can never widen it (ADR-082).
%%   * Sub-agents. The delegation hop architecture-future.mmd has drawn
%%     since Week 1 becomes real: delegate is a tool on the same registry,
%%     and a child is another AgentLoop with its own context and its own
%%     registry — which is why loop.py does not change for it either.
%%   * Traces. The JSONL exporter, one file per run, holding the span tree.
%%     Metrics answer "how is it doing"; the trace answers "what did this
%%     one run do". An optional OTLP exporter sends the same spans to
%%     Jaeger, off by default and unable to fail a run (ADR-095).
%%   * Task quality, kept apart from run success. A run can answer and
%%     still not have done what was asked, so a verdict is recorded
%%     against the run id rather than derived (ADR-096).
%%   * A budget gate on the model call. Every chat() — the parent's and each
%%     child's — goes through one BudgetedLLMClient, so a rolling 24-hour
%%     window and a per-prompt checkpoint are enforced in one place and
%%     loop.py knows nothing about either (ADR-088, ADR-089). The per-prompt
%%     stop is a pause: the user types "continue" and the same task resumes.
%%   * The memory write path. Every long-term write — the memory tools,
%%     /remember, and an extraction pass over the user's own message at run
%%     end — goes through ONE MemoryWriter, which consolidates it against
%%     what is stored: a correction supersedes the old fact, never deletes
%%     it (ADR-107). Its model calls, like extraction's and the
%%     conversation summary's, go through the same budgeted, traced client
%%     as the agent's.
%%   * Conversation folding. A long REPL chat is folded into a rolling
%%     summary at the start of a turn, cutting only at user messages so no
%%     tool call loses its result (ADR-108).
%%   * A claim check on the agent's model calls. A final answer that says
%%     "I have created ..." when no tool ran this turn is sent back once;
%%     the model then acts or corrects itself (ADR-116).
%%   * Delegation decided at run time. At the first read of a turn the
%%     coordinator's client asks the model whether the request splits into
%%     independent parts; a yes reaches the loop as a delegate(tasks=[...])
%%     call, dispatched and gated like any other (ADR-117).
%%   * Short-term memory. One markdown file the agent writes itself,
%%     injected whole every run. It is outside the context window, so
%%     compaction — which now shrinks tool-call ARGUMENTS as well as
%%     results, and lists what it removed — cannot reach it (ADR-090).
%% ---
%% The LIFECYCLE box is drawn as one trunk rather than an arrow from every
%% phase, which is not an artistic choice: the loop really does call one
%% CompositeHook, and that object is the only thing it knows about. Seven
%% observers behind it is a fan-out the loop cannot see.
%% ---
%% Note the ordering, which is load-bearing rather than cosmetic: telemetry
%% is FIRST so its agent.run span encloses every other hook's work, and
%% CompositeHook unwinds on_run_end in reverse so it also closes last.
%% Composed the other way round, the memory hook opened a span with nothing
%% on the tracer stack and wrote a second trace file for the same run.
%% ---
%% Boxes are runtime phases and processes, not Python packages —
%% architecture.md maps each box to its module.
flowchart TB
    User([User])
    CLI["CLI / User Interface
    banner names every root, the policy, the metrics URL"]
    Response["Final Response"]

    User -->|"Task"| CLI
    CLI -->|"User Request"| Planner

    subgraph AgentSystem["AGENT SYSTEM — one AgentLoop, unchanged since Week 1"]
        direction TB
        Planner["Planner / Main Agent
        role = main
        • Understand task
        • Create and update plan
        • Process tool feedback
        • Decide next step or finish"]
        Context["Context
        • Task · plan · previous results
        • Injected memory, skills and working notes
        • Today's date and the week ahead
        • Compaction: stubs old results AND old
          tool-call payloads, then lists what it took"]
        Reasoning["Reasoning / Tool Selection
        • Decide what to do next
        • Select tool from Registry"]
        Planner --> Context
        Context --> Reasoning
    end

    subgraph ModelGate["MODEL GATE — one place, before every model call"]
        direction TB
        Planner2["DelegationPlanner — the coordinator only
        at the first read of a turn asks ONE question:
        does this split into independent parts?
        yes → the loop gets delegate(tasks=[…]) (ADR-117)"]
        Grounding["GroundingLLMClient — the agent's calls only
        a final answer that claims an action
        with no tool result this turn is
        sent back ONCE (ADR-116)"]
        Budgeted["BudgetedLLMClient
        wraps the real client, built once in session.py
        • window spent → BudgetExceeded
        • instruction spent → PromptBudgetExceeded
        charges the ledger with what the reply reports"]
        ChatClient["OpenAICompatibleClient
        InnKube · Gemini · OpenAI · Groq · Ollama …
        the only HTTP call the harness makes"]
        Planner2 --> Grounding
        Grounding --> Budgeted
        Budgeted -->|"allowed"| ChatClient
    end

    subgraph Gate["PERMISSION GATE — one place, before every tool call"]
        direction TB
        SkillScope["SkillScopedPolicy
        a loaded skill's allowed-tools
        narrows the set, never widens it
        off by default"]
        Policy["PermissionPolicy
        risk tiers · deny-list · confirm tier
        allow · deny · require_user_confirmation"]
        Confirmer["Confirmer
        asks on the terminal: yes · no
        allow for session · deny for session
        re-asks a typo, fails closed with no terminal"]
        SkillScope --> Policy
        Policy -.->|"confirm tier"| Confirmer
    end

    subgraph Execution["TOOL EXECUTION — one flat list, whatever the origin"]
        direction TB
        Tools["Tool Registry & Execution
        • File tools — workspace root
        • Memory tools — no path, a collection
        • skill_read — skills root
        • Remote MCP tools — server-prefixed
        • delegate — a tool like any other"]
        SubAgent["Sub-Agents — researcher | writer | critic
        • own system prompt, own RunContext
        • own registry, derived from capabilities
        • own policy and budget, never wider than the parent's
        • own deadline, checked at each model call
        • up to subagent_max_concurrency at once, in a worker pool
        • no delegate: no role holds the capability
        • returns a VALIDATED structured result"]
        McpClient["MCP Client — one per server
        • Launch over stdio or connect over http
        • Discover tools at runtime
        • Refuse destructive tools, then register
        • Restart a dead session once"]
        Tools -->|"delegate(role, task) or delegate(tasks=[...])
        — independent tasks fan out concurrently"| SubAgent
        SubAgent -->|"its own registry, minus delegate"| Tools
        Tools -.->|"time_plus__ / calendar__ / web__"| McpClient
    end

    subgraph Remote["MCP SERVERS — one subprocess each, config.yaml only"]
        direction TB
        TimeServer["mcp_server_time_plus
        forked from the reference server
        • get_current_time · convert_time
        • find_meeting_slot · count_working_days"]
        CalendarServer["mcp_server_calendar
        forked from ics-calendar-mcp
        • get_events_today · get_events_range
        • get_event_details · search_events
        • list_recurring_events
        • create_event · suggest_reschedule_slots"]
        WebServer["mcp_server_web_search
        • web_search · web_fetch"]
        CalendarStore[("Calendar volume
        calendar/calendar.ics
        a local file, not a feed URL")]
        CalendarServer -->|"reads / writes .ics"| CalendarStore
    end

    Lifecycle["LIFECYCLE — one CompositeHook
    on_run_start · before_llm · after_llm · on_llm_error
    before_tool · after_permission · after_tool · on_run_end"]

    subgraph Observers["OBSERVERS — the loop knows none of them by name"]
        direction TB
        ConversationHook["ConversationSummaryHook — SECOND
        folds turns older than the last few into
        a rolling summary once over budget (ADR-108)"]
        MemoryHook["MemoryHook
        injects facts, writes the run summary"]
        ExtractHook["MemoryExtractionHook
        at run end, reads the USER's message only
        and proposes facts to the MemoryWriter (ADR-107)"]
        SkillsHook["SkillsHook
        injects the skill index"]
        NotesHook["NotesHook
        injects the working notes, whole,
        at run start AND before each request
        when the file changed (ADR-105)"]
        Telemetry["TelemetryHook — FIRST, so its span encloses the rest
        opens agent.run · agent.iteration · llm.call
        tool.call · permission.check · memory.* · subagent.run
        one instrumentation point, no stopwatches anywhere else"]
        ConsoleHook["ConsoleTraceHook
        the arrows a human watches"]
    end

    subgraph Persistence["PERSISTENT STATE — outside the workspace"]
        direction TB
        Writer["MemoryWriter — every long-term write
        exact repeat → skip · judge: add / update / duplicate
        update = new record + supersede the old one
        user outranks harness outranks agent"]
        Memory[("Qdrant — agent_memory
        core_fact · project_note
        cosine + recency decay · superseded hidden
        core facts: every one up to 10, relevant first (ADR-118)")]
        Writer --> Memory
        Skills[("Skills
        SKILL.md bundles, read-only")]
        SessionLog[("Run log
        memory/sessions.md")]
        Traces[("Traces
        memory/traces/*.jsonl
        memory/traces/delegations/*.json")]
        Notes[("Working notes
        memory/notes.md
        the agent's own state for this task")]
        Ledger[("Budget ledger
        memory/budget.json
        window start · spend · credit")]
    end

    Tracer["TRACER — one stack of open spans PER THREAD
    trace_id IS the run id · parentage is the stack
    a concurrent child adopts its parent's span, so the
    tree still joins across the worker boundary
    an exporter that raises loses a span, never a run"]

    subgraph Exporters["EXPORTERS — one span in, three sinks out"]
        direction TB
        JsonlExp["JsonlSpanExporter
        one file per run, span tree
        v1 keys kept · schema_version: 2"]
        MetricsExp["MetricsSpanExporter
        spans to counters
        25 names · no run_id label"]
        OtlpExp["OtlpSpanExporter
        OPTIONAL, off by default
        gen_ai.* semconv · batched off-thread"]
    end

    subgraph Observability["OBSERVABILITY — scraped, never pushed"]
        direction TB
        Exporter["/metrics on :9091
        a closed port is a banner line, not a crash"]
        Prometheus["Prometheus
        scrapes harness:9091 · 5 alert rules"]
        Grafana["Grafana
        row 0: failures BY LAYER — the panel you open first
        rows 1-7: the brief's bullets
        rows 8-11: diagnosis · context · memory · task quality"]
        Jaeger["Jaeger — optional
        the same run as a flame graph
        found by the id the banner printed"]
        Exporter -->|"HTTP pull"| Prometheus
        Prometheus --> Grafana
    end

    %% Every model call, the parent's and each child's, through one client.
    Planner -->|"chat(messages, tools)"| Planner2
    Budgeted <-->|"charge · read"| Ledger
    Budgeted -.->|"budget stop — the REPL survives;
    'continue' resumes, 'use credit on the go' overrides"| CLI
    SubAgent -.->|"the same client instance"| Grounding

    %% The act half of the cycle: propose, gate, execute, feed back.
    Reasoning -->|"Proposed tool call"| SkillScope
    Policy -->|"allow · confirmed"| Tools
    Policy -.->|"deny · declined — a refusal is an observation,
    and counts as a failure for that tool"| Planner
    Tools -->|"Result / Error Feedback"| Planner
    SubAgent -->|"DelegationResult — status, validated payload,
    summary clipped to budget, path to the full record"| Planner
    SubAgent -.->|"its own run_start / llm / tool / run_end"| Lifecycle

    %% Tools that reach state, and the one that narrows the gate.
    Tools -->|"memory tools"| Writer
    CLI -->|"/remember"| Writer
    ExtractHook -->|"proposed facts"| Writer
    Writer -.->|"judge call"| Budgeted
    ExtractHook -.->|"extract call"| Budgeted
    ConversationHook -.->|"summary call"| Budgeted
    Tools -->|"note_write · note_append"| Notes
    Tools -->|"skill_read narrows the gate
    until /reset"| SkillScope
    McpClient <-->|"MCP over stdin / stdout"| TimeServer
    McpClient <-->|"MCP over stdin / stdout"| CalendarServer
    McpClient <-->|"MCP over stdin / stdout"| WebServer

    %% The observe half: one trunk in, five observers out.
    Planner -.-> Lifecycle
    Gate -.-> Lifecycle
    Tools -.-> Lifecycle
    Lifecycle --> Telemetry
    Lifecycle --> ConversationHook
    Lifecycle --> MemoryHook
    Lifecycle --> ExtractHook
    Lifecycle --> SkillsHook
    Lifecycle --> NotesHook
    Lifecycle --> ConsoleHook
    Telemetry -->|"opens / closes spans"| Tracer
    MemoryHook -.->|"memory.read / memory.write
    the retrieval that goes through no tool call"| Tracer
    Tracer --> JsonlExp
    Tracer --> MetricsExp
    Tracer -.-> OtlpExp

    Memory -.->|"query on the task"| MemoryHook
    Skills -.->|"index at startup"| SkillsHook
    Notes -.->|"read at run start and per request"| NotesHook
    ConversationHook -->|"fold · summary section"| Context
    MemoryHook -->|"inject"| Context
    SkillsHook -->|"inject"| Context
    NotesHook -->|"inject"| Context
    MemoryHook -->|"summary at run end"| SessionLog
    JsonlExp --> Traces
    MetricsExp --> Exporter
    OtlpExp -.->|"OTLP/HTTP :4318"| Jaeger

    Planner -->|"Task Complete"| Response
    Response --> CLI
    CLI --> User

